From: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau/bios: map the NV40 shader PLL for limit lookups

NV4x boards with differing core and shader clocks in their performance
table (e.g. G70 / GeForce 7800 GT: core 375 MHz, shader 400 MHz) drive
the shader/ROP domain from the second PLL at 0x004008. nv40_clk_calc()
looks up the limits of that PLL by register, but nv40_pll_mapping[]
lacks an entry for it, so pll_map_reg() fails and nvbios_pll_parse()
returns -ENOENT. The core and shader clocks are then never changed,
while the memory clock and voltage of the new performance level are
applied, e.g. on a PowerMac G5 7800 GT after selecting pstate 0x21:

  21: core 375 MHz shader 400 MHz memory 1000 MHz AC DC *
  AC: core 275 MHz shader 275 MHz memory 1000 MHz

The BIT 'C' PLL limits table (v0x21) of such boards carries a dedicated
0x004008 entry (VCO 400-800 MHz), which the lookup by register finds
once the PLL is mapped. Tables without one fall back to the first
entry, as already done for the core PLL.

Also report a failed PLL limits lookup in nv40_clk_calc_pll(), which
so far returned without any message, like nv40_ram_calc() already does
for the memory PLL.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/bios/pll.c |    2 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/nv40.c |    5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/bios/pll.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/bios/pll.c
@@ -45,6 +46,7 @@ nv04_pll_mapping[] = {
 static struct pll_mapping
 nv40_pll_mapping[] = {
 	{ PLL_CORE  , 0x004000 },
+	{ PLL_SHADER, 0x004008 },
 	{ PLL_MEMORY, 0x004020 },
 	{ PLL_VPLL0 , 0x680508 },
 	{ PLL_VPLL1 , 0x680520 },
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/nv40.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/nv40.c
@@ -129,8 +130,10 @@ nv40_clk_calc_pll(struct nv40_clk *clk,
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = nvbios_pll_parse(subdev->device->bios, reg, &pll);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		nvkm_error(subdev, "pll %06x limits not found: %d\n", reg, ret);
 		return ret;
+	}
 
 	if (khz < pll.vco1.max_freq)
 		pll.vco2.max_freq = 0;
